You are sober,

260
00:13:02,515 --> 00:13:03,917
London.

261
00:13:12,692 --> 00:13:15,128
Hello, Mr. Officer.

262
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:17,097
What seems to be the problem?

263
00:13:18,598 --> 00:13:21,034
Appears you have
an illegal tint.

264
00:13:21,034 --> 00:13:22,702
Really?

265
00:13:22,702 --> 00:13:25,205
I'm sorry, this my mama car.

266
00:13:25,205 --> 00:13:28,041
Your mother drives
a murdered-out Nissan Altima?

267
00:13:28,041 --> 00:13:30,911
I know. My mom,

268
00:13:30,911 --> 00:13:33,046
she got to stunt on them.

269
00:13:35,215 --> 00:13:36,549
Have you been drinking
today, ma'am?

270
00:13:36,549 --> 00:13:38,585
Of course not.

271
00:13:38,585 --> 00:13:41,054
What's that right there?
- Water.

272
00:13:41,054 --> 00:13:43,556
- Really?
- Yeah.

273
00:13:44,724 --> 00:13:46,726
Yeah, if it were vodka,
would I do this?

274
00:13:46,726 --> 00:13:48,061
Whoa...

275
00:13:59,907 --> 00:14:01,741
Whoo!

276
00:14:05,578 --> 00:14:07,280
Step out of the vehicle, ma'am.

277
00:14:11,985 --> 00:14:13,921
Act white, just...

278
00:14:15,588 --> 00:14:17,324
Step over to the curb
for me, please.

279
00:14:21,995 --> 00:14:23,763
Walk a straight line.

280
00:14:29,436 --> 00:14:31,504
Arms out wide.

281
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:35,775
Touch the tip of your nose
with your forefinger.

282
00:14:39,779 --> 00:14:43,150
How many seasons of Homeboys
in Outer Space were there?

283
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:45,018
One.

284
00:14:48,989 --> 00:14:50,657
You have a nice day, ma'am.

285
00:14:50,657 --> 00:14:53,893
- What?
- Thank you.

286
00:14:57,630 --> 00:14:59,899
10-4. All clear.

287
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,334
Hey!

288
00:15:01,334 --> 00:15:02,802
Whoa! Whoa, whoa, whoa! Wait!

289
00:15:02,802 --> 00:15:04,304
What're you doing with... Hey!

290
00:15:04,304 --> 00:15:06,639
Are you crazy?
What are... what're you doing?

291
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:08,141
I don't know. Let's go.

292
00:15:08,141 --> 00:15:09,642
How'd you even do that?
Like...

293
00:15:09,642 --> 00:15:12,179
Whoa!

294
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:16,149
What?

295
00:15:16,149 --> 00:15:17,817
- I'm sorry!
- What-what--
Where are you going?

296
00:15:17,817 --> 00:15:20,653
I'm sorry!
This is all your fault!

297
00:15:20,653 --> 00:15:22,322
What do you mean? Oh!

298
00:15:30,497 --> 00:15:32,165
You okay?

299
00:15:36,036 --> 00:15:38,838
Yeah, I'm fine. I...

300
00:15:38,838 --> 00:15:40,840
I guess I just kind of...

301
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,343
freaked out a little bit.
It's all right.

302
00:15:43,343 --> 00:15:44,844
No, it's-it's all good.

303
00:15:44,844 --> 00:15:46,546
It happens.

304
00:15:46,546 --> 00:15:48,415
Would you like to take a break
in the tearoom?

305
00:15:50,383 --> 00:15:53,186
Yes, tearoom. Let's do that.

306
00:15:59,426 --> 00:16:01,294
Whew...

307
00:16:03,530 --> 00:16:05,198
I'll fetch you some tea
in the tearoom

308
00:16:05,198 --> 00:16:07,534
while you go relax
in the tearoom.

309
00:16:35,295 --> 00:16:36,896
Oh, thanks.

310
00:16:36,896 --> 00:16:38,431
You're welcome.

311
00:16:38,431 --> 00:16:40,233
Is this your first time?

312
00:16:41,901 --> 00:16:44,003
No, actually, I, uh,

313
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:46,406
come here once a week.

314
00:16:46,406 --> 00:16:48,575
Cleanses my spirit.

315
00:16:48,575 --> 00:16:50,677
Mm. I know.

316
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:53,012
My favorite part is the tearoom.

317
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,514
The tea in the tearoom

318
00:16:54,514 --> 00:16:57,084
- is amazing for sure.
- Mm.

319
00:16:59,286 --> 00:17:01,854
W-Why do y'all
keep saying "tearoom"?

320
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:06,526
Be-Because it's the tearoom.

321
00:17:31,318 --> 00:17:34,053
Oh, my gosh. What is happening?

322
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:36,223
Wake up!

323
00:17:36,223 --> 00:17:38,325
- I-I don't understand. I...
- Don't come back.

324
00:17:38,325 --> 00:17:41,461
Hey. Hey, man,
I thought it was a dream.

325
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:44,697
Damn.

326
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:58,245
How's the chicken skin salad
going?

327
00:17:58,245 --> 00:18:00,647
It's salty, man.

328
00:18:00,647 --> 00:18:02,849
But not salty enough.

329
00:18:05,152 --> 00:18:08,421
Excellent. Well, I'll be
right back with your next dish.

330
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:09,689
Let me take this
out of the way for you.

331
00:18:09,689 --> 00:18:11,591
- Thank you.
- I'll take that, too.

332
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,593
- Thank you.
- No problem.

333
00:18:17,864 --> 00:18:19,866
Can we please
get the hell out of here?

334
00:18:19,866 --> 00:18:22,502
What? No. We're not
doing that to them.

335
00:18:22,502 --> 00:18:27,174
The rice has corn in it.
I just can't.

336
00:18:27,174 --> 00:18:28,175
I fuck with
the yellow rice, okay?

337
00:18:28,175 --> 00:18:29,842
Uh, points for the idea.

338
00:18:29,842 --> 00:18:32,345
This shit is gross.

339
00:18:32,345 --> 00:18:34,714
It's gross, man.

340
00:18:34,714 --> 00:18:36,349
That chef over there
is making sushi rolls

341
00:18:36,349 --> 00:18:38,050
with his bare-ass hands, Earn.

342
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:40,787
♪ Or one of us will leave here
tonight in a hearse ♪

343
00:18:40,787 --> 00:18:42,789
♪ When we'll be tried by 12
and fertilizing daisies... ♪

344
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:45,792
Yeah, the fish is raw,
but it's warm.

345
00:18:45,792 --> 00:18:47,894
Like, I feel like
that can't be safe.

346
00:18:47,894 --> 00:18:49,529
Can we please...
can we just please

347
00:18:49,529 --> 00:18:52,299
just go across the street, man,
get lunch real quick,

348
00:18:52,299 --> 00:18:53,800
and stop lying
to these Black folk?

349
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:57,136
It's a Black sushi
fusion restaurant, okay?

350
00:18:57,136 --> 00:19:00,873
There's gonna be a couple of
new ideas thrown at you, okay?

351
00:19:00,873 --> 00:19:03,710
Can we please
keep our minds open?

352
00:19:03,710 --> 00:19:06,646
Could I interest you on a refill
of, uh, hot white Hennessy?

353
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:08,715
♪ 'Cause I'd rather be
tried by 12... ♪

354
00:19:08,715 --> 00:19:10,717
I need, I need, I need, uh,
I need the bathroom, man.

355
00:19:10,717 --> 00:19:12,552
- Yeah, yeah, I gotcha.
- Uh, uh, got me on that?

356
00:19:12,552 --> 00:19:14,887
All right. Cool. I'm-a just...
I'm-a run to the bathroom.

357
00:19:14,887 --> 00:19:17,224
So we might catch a body... ♪

358
00:19:17,224 --> 00:19:19,559
- Hey.
- Be careful.

359
00:19:19,559 --> 00:19:20,827
- You got it, man?
- Hey, I'm good, man. I'm good.

360
00:19:20,827 --> 00:19:22,229
All right.

361
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:36,075
Oh.

362
00:19:51,924 --> 00:19:53,960
Hey, man.

363
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:56,629
Yo. What are you doing here?

364
00:19:56,629 --> 00:19:58,531
Uh, I just was
in the neighborhood,

365
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:00,700
and, um, thought I'd come by.

366
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:02,769
You lying.

367
00:20:06,005 --> 00:20:07,540
- Hey.
- Come on.

368
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:08,975
- What's up, man?
- What's up?

369
00:20:08,975 --> 00:20:10,977
- Is it okay if I hug you?
- Of course, man.

370
00:20:10,977 --> 00:20:13,212
- All right.
- Can't get no sicker.

371
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,647
All right.

372
00:20:14,647 --> 00:20:16,816
- Come in, bro.
- Yo.

373
00:20:16,816 --> 00:20:19,486
- Ugh.
- I was just, um...

374
00:20:19,486 --> 00:20:21,354
Got something for you.

375
00:20:22,522 --> 00:20:24,491
You know they deliver, right?

376
00:20:24,491 --> 00:20:26,993
Yeah. I mean,
I got the app on my phone,

377
00:20:26,993 --> 00:20:29,629
lets me know, so I just thought
I'd help you out.

378
00:20:29,629 --> 00:20:32,999
- Ah. Well, that's nice.
- Yeah, well...

379
00:20:32,999 --> 00:20:36,469
- Oh, come have this jollof.
- Yeah. Uh...

380
00:20:36,469 --> 00:20:38,805
Wait. Wait. Who made jollof?

381
00:20:38,805 --> 00:20:40,340
My roommate, bro.

382
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:41,808
Who the hell
you think made it?

383
00:20:41,808 --> 00:20:43,175
Like, come on.

384
00:20:45,144 --> 00:20:49,148
Um, I can't really
have any right now,

385
00:20:49,148 --> 00:20:51,318
'cause I'm about to go meet up
with some people,

386
00:20:51,318 --> 00:20:52,819
get some food, so...

387
00:20:52,819 --> 00:20:55,355
Wait, you're not staying?

388
00:20:58,325 --> 00:21:01,661
I'm kidding.
It's cool. Don't worry about it.

389
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:05,365
I mean, I'll stay
if you want me to.

390
00:21:05,365 --> 00:21:09,669
Oh, boy, I don't want you
in here. I want you out there.

391
00:21:09,669 --> 00:21:12,505
Have fun. Go see your people.

392
00:21:12,505 --> 00:21:14,607
Great. Now I got the picture...

393
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:19,178
I'll take half a bowl of jollof.

394
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:23,950
Okay. I'm gonna get you
a full bowl.

395
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:26,786
- Just eat half.
- Okay. Thank you.

396
00:21:26,786 --> 00:21:28,521
What else do you want?

397
00:21:50,910 --> 00:21:53,279
I miss you, man.

398
00:21:54,614 --> 00:21:56,282
Miss you.

399
00:21:58,918 --> 00:22:00,453
How's Mom?

400
00:22:06,826 --> 00:22:08,595
What about Dad?

401
00:22:11,398 --> 00:22:13,299
Yeah.

402
00:22:20,139 --> 00:22:23,342
...to get
a check cut and sent to us.

403
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,845
Pay your son's bills.
The case is dismissed.

404
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:28,347
They sound like very nice
people to me. Outrageous.

405
00:22:31,017 --> 00:22:32,485
Whoa.

406
00:22:35,154 --> 00:22:37,524
Damn.

407
00:22:42,128 --> 00:22:44,697
Are you okay?

408
00:22:44,697 --> 00:22:47,133
Hey, I thought you said I
couldn't turn over in here, man.

409
00:22:47,133 --> 00:22:49,301
I-I've never seen that before.

410
00:22:50,269 --> 00:22:52,304
Wait.

411
00:22:52,304 --> 00:22:54,641
How long was I asleep?

412
00:22:54,641 --> 00:22:57,109
I-I don't know.
About 30 minoots?

413
00:22:57,109 --> 00:22:58,878
Maybe 35.

414
00:22:58,878 --> 00:23:00,312
Wait. Wait. What?

415
00:23:00,312 --> 00:23:02,949
30 minoo...!

416
00:23:23,736 --> 00:23:25,738
You were gone for a while, man.

417
00:23:25,738 --> 00:23:27,173
Yeah, man. That's 'cause, uh,

418
00:23:27,173 --> 00:23:28,675
the bathroom was in the Rainbow
across the street.

419
00:23:28,675 --> 00:23:30,342
Damn.

420
00:23:30,342 --> 00:23:32,311
- I'm going to Popeyes right now.
- What?

421
00:23:32,311 --> 00:23:34,180
Wait. We still have
the main meal.

422
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:35,682
Hey, do you know
what time it is?

423
00:23:35,682 --> 00:23:37,484
You know what time it is?
It is 2:55 p.m.

424
00:23:37,484 --> 00:23:39,151
That means, in five minutes,
that Popeyes across the street

425
00:23:39,151 --> 00:23:40,687
is gonna be filled
with goddamn high schoolers.

426
00:23:40,687 --> 00:23:42,354
And our only chance of getting
a goddamn chicken sandwich

427
00:23:42,354 --> 00:23:44,691
is gonna be goddamn next week,
so I'm out, goddamn it.

428
00:23:44,691 --> 00:23:46,659
- How was the bathroom, sir?
- Far, nigga. It was far.

429
00:23:46,659 --> 00:23:48,828
Well, uh, we have a surprise
for you guys today.

430
00:23:48,828 --> 00:23:50,697
It's the, uh, chef's special--

431
00:23:50,697 --> 00:23:52,999
a very rare delicacy,
especially here in Georgia.

432
00:23:52,999 --> 00:23:54,701
Blowfish cheek.

433
00:23:54,701 --> 00:23:56,168
And as you all have
probably heard,

434
00:23:56,168 --> 00:23:58,170
blowfish are extremely poisonous

435
00:23:58,170 --> 00:24:00,339
and must be cut
with a skilled hand.

436
00:24:00,339 --> 00:24:02,709
But Chef Kenny--
he studied with the finest,

437
00:24:02,709 --> 00:24:04,511
and Demarcus oversaw
the cutting himself.

438
00:24:04,511 --> 00:24:07,213
Itadakimasu.

439
00:24:11,250 --> 00:24:13,352
Yeah, I ain't doing that, man.

440
00:24:13,352 --> 00:24:15,354
- I'm sorry?
- I said I'm not doing it!

441
00:24:15,354 --> 00:24:17,456
All right, look, thank y'all
for your service and everything.

442
00:24:17,456 --> 00:24:18,891
The ambiance is beautiful,
the art is great,

443
00:24:18,891 --> 00:24:20,527
but we... we got to go.

444
00:24:20,527 --> 00:24:23,530
But, sir, the-the blowfish is
a rare delicacy. I can assure...

445
00:24:23,530 --> 00:24:25,464
Yeah, man. I'm sure it is.
I'm sure it is, but we got...

446
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:27,634
I got a rap thing
that we got to go to, so, we...

447
00:24:27,634 --> 00:24:29,536
- We double-booked.
- Yeah, sorry about that.

448
00:24:29,536 --> 00:24:31,638
You're going to Popeyes.

449
00:24:31,638 --> 00:24:33,773
Aren't you?

450
00:24:35,041 --> 00:24:37,043
No, man. No.

451
00:24:37,043 --> 00:24:39,045
Yes, you are.

452
00:24:39,045 --> 00:24:41,480
They all do.

453
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,716
Look, I don't know what
you're talking about, man.

454
00:24:43,716 --> 00:24:46,218
- We-we got to rap thing...
- You know,

455
00:24:46,218 --> 00:24:51,257
there's a movie theater
two blocks away from here.

456
00:24:51,257 --> 00:24:54,226
The night
Queen Slim premiered,

457
00:24:54,226 --> 00:24:56,563
we were filled.

458
00:24:56,563 --> 00:24:58,765
Line out the door.

459
00:24:58,765 --> 00:25:01,100
Black people hopped up

460
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:04,637
on nationalism
coming to support their own.

461
00:25:05,938 --> 00:25:08,340
15 minutes later,

462
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:10,743
we were empty.

463
00:25:12,411 --> 00:25:15,848
Not one person ate the blowfish.

464
00:25:15,848 --> 00:25:18,284
Not one.

465
00:25:18,284 --> 00:25:20,352
Just a bunch of Yelp reviews

466
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:22,589
that all said the same thing.

467
00:25:22,589 --> 00:25:25,692
"This nigga serving
poison fish."

468
00:25:25,692 --> 00:25:27,694
- Hey, listen, man. I...
- Do you know

469
00:25:27,694 --> 00:25:31,964
the traditional way to make
sushi is with your bare hands?

470
00:25:32,932 --> 00:25:36,969
And that sushi should be served
at room temperature?

471
00:25:38,337 --> 00:25:40,807
Every Japanese sushi restaurant

472
00:25:40,807 --> 00:25:44,777
worth its soy sauce
does it that way,

473
00:25:44,777 --> 00:25:47,814
and no one seemed to notice.

474
00:25:47,814 --> 00:25:51,117
But if a brother

475
00:25:51,117 --> 00:25:56,623
from Alabama
does it the same way,

476
00:25:56,623 --> 00:25:58,991
suddenly, the fish is dirty.

477
00:25:58,991 --> 00:26:02,394
- Yeah, but y'all serving us...
- You know, in Japan,

478
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,130
there's a sushi restaurant

479
00:26:04,130 --> 00:26:05,665
that can't even
take reservations

480
00:26:05,665 --> 00:26:08,835
from the general public
because it is so acclaimed?

481
00:26:08,835 --> 00:26:11,337
You want to know where it is?

482
00:26:11,337 --> 00:26:16,475
It's on the Ginza line
in a Tokyo subway station.

483
00:26:16,475 --> 00:26:18,477
I know because my master,

484
00:26:18,477 --> 00:26:21,213
Yuji Watanabe, studied there.

485
00:26:22,481 --> 00:26:24,483
You see, he taught me

486
00:26:24,483 --> 00:26:27,654
that it doesn't matter
where you serve the sushi.

487
00:26:27,654 --> 00:26:30,189
A subway,

488
00:26:30,189 --> 00:26:33,826
- an old Blockbuster Video.
- I knew it.

489
00:26:33,826 --> 00:26:35,995
It doesn't matter.

490
00:26:35,995 --> 00:26:40,432
He says, if the sushi's good,

491
00:26:40,432 --> 00:26:42,735
people will come.

492
00:26:45,337 --> 00:26:48,174
But I guess my master was never
a nigga from Florida.

493
00:26:48,174 --> 00:26:51,510
- Listen, brother man.
- Don't give me
that "brother" shit!

494
00:27:00,753 --> 00:27:02,889
This entire dinner,

495
00:27:02,889 --> 00:27:05,692
you have been staring
across the street

496
00:27:05,692 --> 00:27:07,727
at a modern-day Coon Chicken,

497
00:27:07,727 --> 00:27:11,864
served to you by an Aunt Jemima,

498
00:27:11,864 --> 00:27:14,033
who lies to you repeatedly,

499
00:27:14,033 --> 00:27:16,202
telling you it is her recipe

500
00:27:16,202 --> 00:27:19,038
and that she is benefiting
from it.

501
00:27:19,038 --> 00:27:21,473
It is not her recipe.

502
00:27:21,473 --> 00:27:24,210
You know who owns that recipe?

503
00:27:24,210 --> 00:27:28,214
An Italian man and his family,

504
00:27:28,214 --> 00:27:30,549
none of which
have married Black.

505
00:27:30,549 --> 00:27:35,054
I heard some of them even moved
from New Orleans to New Jersey.

506
00:27:36,889 --> 00:27:39,726
New... Jersey.

507
00:27:39,726 --> 00:27:41,728
All right, man.

508
00:27:41,728 --> 00:27:43,730
All right, I get it.

509
00:27:43,730 --> 00:27:45,397
Oh, you get it?

510
00:27:45,397 --> 00:27:47,599
Yeah. Yeah, I-I get it.

511
00:27:47,599 --> 00:27:50,269
- You get it now?
- I get it now, man.

512
00:27:51,270 --> 00:27:52,939
Then eat it.

513
00:28:00,412 --> 00:28:02,949
- What?
- Eat it.

514
00:28:02,949 --> 00:28:07,453
- Eat my poison fish, brother.
